{
  "rationale": "Iteration 8 (score 668, best so far) moved sensor y from 0.07 to 0.075 at mass 0.6, body_length 0.10 and wheel_track 0.09. The oval held 20 of 20 finishes with max_error 0.0165, so the extra look-ahead added no lag. The s-bend kept 19 of 20 finishes with oscillation 0.32, under the 0.35 limit. Slalom progress rose from 0.26 to 0.34, but it still has 0 finishes, line losses of 1.1, and max_error at the 0.0648 off-track floor. The s-bend line losses (0.8) did not reach the 0.55 target, so the feedback's keep-y-0.075 condition is only partly met. Across iterations 5 to 8, the geometry levers (inertia, look-ahead, track width, footprint) have each been tested. Their gains are now small: the s-bend has plateaued at 19 of 20 finishes, and the slalom still sits at its floor. The Integrator's feedback says that once the slalom stays at its max_error floor with 0 finishes after the y change, geometry is near its limit and the next step should be controller gain. I therefore hold the iteration 8 geometry exactly, so the next race isolates controller effects for the Integrator. I considered wheel_track 0.095 as a compromise, but it would be a second geometry change while the s-bend and slalom trade off against each other, and it would blur the attribution. Expected result: the same geometry scores about 668 under the Integrator's new controller. Any change in score can then be attributed to the controller.",
